  "body": "## What changed\n\nA STEP closed shell that meshes open (a real gap, e.g. walls missing on a face truck cannot mesh) used to be refused at import (#1576), so the part could not even be loaded for viewing or setup. Now the model import lands it **incomplete**:\n\n- `step_closed::judge` returns the hole, named, instead of refusing; `step::parse_open` and `import::{load,parse}_model_open_within` keep it in `Graded::open`. Every other loader (`load_model`, `parse_model`, `*_graded_within`: fixtures-by-path, tool bodies) still refuses with the same words as before.\n- `ImportModel` (GUI, MCP `import_model`, script `import`) lands the mesh with the fidelity-unknown sentinel (`model_fidelity::UNKNOWN_MM`, #1056) and the hole in a new component `schema::MeshOpen`. The sentinel rides every chord path (stock copies, setup clones, undo, save), so every operation on the model and the program verdict are refused at the post by the existing gate, and the program sim gives no verdict.\n- New module `mesh_open`: the refusal words (\"model 'X' was imported incomplete - closed shell #N (F faces) meshes open: ... - so it has walls missing and no gouge check against it can be trusted; re-export the model, or import an STL\"), the model page / import status line (\"Incomplete: ...\"), and the MCP/script `reduced_fidelity` facts (`incomplete: true`, `hole`).\n- The hole is traded by `UpdateModel` (new `with_hole`, undo restores it; a whole re-import clears it), `DeleteEntity` undo, and the project file (optional entity key `mesh_open`, written only beside `fidelity_unknown`; a `mesh_open` without the mark is refused as corrupt). No project version bump: an old reader drops the key and keeps the mark, so it still refuses (decision file).\n- `model_fidelity::set` clears any hole, so a stale hole never speaks for a whole mesh.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1610-open-shell-incomplete.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests, new suite `crates/app/tests/import_step_open_shell.rs`:\n- `a_closed_shell_that_meshes_open_imports_incomplete_with_its_hole_named` (the bent `fillet_corner.step` fixture: loads, facets present, hole named incl. the dropped face, summary/facts say incomplete; the graded loader still refuses)\n- `every_operation_on_an_incomplete_model_is_refused_at_the_post_naming_the_hole` (verification report, sim not judged, `post_setup` refused, not the pre-v59 note)\n- `the_hole_rides_undo_and_a_whole_reimport_clears_it`\n- `the_hole_rides_the_project_file_and_is_refused_without_its_mark`\n\nUpdated: `step_seams_tests::the_importer_closes_seams_within_two_chord_tolerances_only` (the gap is now returned named, not refused, by `judge`).\n\nMutation checks (each line deleted or neutralised, the two STEP suites run, restored and touched): 17 of 17 red - `MeshOpen` write, the hole in `op_problem` / `verdict_tol` / the fixture line, save / load / validate of `mesh_open`, `ImportModel`'s unknown chord, hole landing and `graded.open`, `UpdateModel` apply and undo, `DeleteEntity` undo, the parser collecting holes, `judge` returning the hole, and both graded loaders still refusing.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): green on 35b3422c (app suites 364 s, ui suites 151 s). Clippy `-p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\nUI review follow-up: `incomplete_model_page_and_import_status_name_the_hole_and_post_refusal` imports the missing-wall STEP box through the real UI import queue. It checks the model page and painted status for the hole, post refusal, and re-export/STL advice, and rejects coarse-model advice. Three mutation checks were RED: restore the old page summary, restore the coarse-advice guard, and restore the old status summary. Each restored source was GREEN.\n\nQuick gate on review-fix head `af106857f85c9173c5ed3633d906824f9a15c985`: green (app 1,472 passed, UI 885 passed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe same missing-wall STEP box is shown before and after. Both images render the shipping shell through its headless egui harness. The viewport is the harness placeholder. No pixel goldens changed.\n\nBefore: the previous graded-loader entry point refuses the input, so no model page exists. This capture temporarily restores that entry point in the current harness.\n\n![Before: import refused, no model available](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/af106857f85c9173c5ed3633d906824f9a15c985/docs/reviews/1699/before.png)\n\nAfter: the current loader imports the model incomplete. The model page and import status name the hole and post refusal. The coarse-model advice is absent.\n\n![After: incomplete model page and import status](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/af106857f85c9173c5ed3633d906824f9a15c985/docs/reviews/1699/after.png)\n\nStructural pin: `incomplete_model_page_and_import_status_name_the_hole_and_post_refusal`. Capture details: [README](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/af106857f85c9173c5ed3633d906824f9a15c985/docs/reviews/1699/README.md).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The user's real-world STEP files that motivated #1576 (local only, not committed).\n- A stock copied from an incomplete model whose source is then deleted: still refused, but its refusal falls back to the pre-v59 words (noted in the decision file).\n\nBranched from upstream/main 058e14ca. Process change: no.\n\nChangelog: A STEP closed shell that meshes open now imports as an incomplete model with its hole named, instead of being refused; every operation on it is refused at the post by name.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1610\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
